<main class="english-magazine"><nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/en/">English edition</a><span>/</span><span>Cultural magazine</span></nav><header><p class="eyebrow">MARTINFIERRO.ORG · THE ENGLISH EDITION</p><h1>Culture, history, and <em>the gaucho world</em></h1><p class="intro">The story of Martín Fierro opens onto a much larger country: its rural workplaces, social gatherings, political struggles and cultural memory. These independent English-language essays explore that world through documented historical sources.</p></header><section aria-label="Published cultural essays" class="stories">{articles.map(a=><article class="story"><a href={a.url}><img src={a.image} alt={a.alt} loading="lazy"/><div><h2>{a.title}</h2><p>{a.summary}</p><span>Read the article ↗</span></div></a></article>)}</section><section class="note"><h2>What this collection is</h2><p>Each article is written for readers of English and has its own historical focus. Some themes overlap with the Spanish magazine, but the editions grow independently. Only published articles appear here, and illustrations are distinguished from authentic archival documents.</p><p><a href="/en/archive/">Explore historical documents</a> · <a href="/en/characters/">Meet the characters</a></p></section></main>
